## Viewing versus cost
Streaming services weigh how many people start and finish a series against what it costs. Expensive shows need bigger audiences.

## Subscribers matter most
Platforms want shows that attract new subscribers or keep existing ones. A series that does neither is at risk.

## Contracts and timing
Cast and crew costs often rise after a season or two, which makes renewal pricier just as the novelty fades.

## What to watch
Watching soon after release and finishing the season helps, because early viewing is generally what services weigh most.
